"""
Public guided-program contracts.

Implementation packages declare reviewed card topology, bounded choices, source-backed support identifiers and progress
policy. Hees.ai validates those declarations, evaluates the original learner operation, and—through the terminal
evaluator—derives the one admitted card, selected support, Content DNA, and receipt an application may inspect.

The module does not load package files, retrieve additional memory, render cards, call a model, or mutate durable
progress. A caller-supplied frame or nomination cannot manufacture authority; the terminal evaluator derives support
only from the installed package projection.
"""

pub from crate.program.decision import ProgramEvaluation
pub from crate.program.terminal_evaluation import evaluate_program_terminal, validate_program_authority_package
pub from crate.program.evaluation import evaluate_program_action
